d":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Describe the bug**\r\nMax decimals for drag value seems to not be working on master? Maxes out at 2-4 seemingly random.\r\n![drag_value_max_decimals](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/7019130/204860454-a26050e4-0389-4b00-91c5-84d3e9e5015d.gif)\r\n\r\n**To Reproduce**\r\nSteps to reproduce the behavior:\r\n1. Change the hello_world example to use:\r\n    ``` rust\r\n    ui.add(\r\n        egui::DragValue::new(&mut self.height)\r\n            .min_decimals(1)\r\n            .max_decimals(10),\r\n    );\r\n    ```\r\n2. Add a height f32 to the `MyApp` struct.\r\n3. Try to enter a value with 10 decimals\r\n4. Observe that you cannot get past 2-4 decimal places.\r\n\r\n**Expected behavior**\r\nIt should allow you to enter more decimal places like it did in 0.19.0\r\n\r\n**Desktop (please complete the following information):**\r\n - OS: Windows\r\n - Version: 11 22H2 22621.819\r\n\r\n**Additional context**\r\nMight be related to the recent change to dragvalue in 0336816faf9f361e59ca77f99c19fcfa2bf7c993 which will be greatly appreciated and is the reason I tried out master, but for my application I'll need to be able to enter higher precision values sometimes.\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"emilk","id":1148717,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNDg3MTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1148717?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilk","html_url":"https://github.com/emilk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/emilk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.gi